{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+t⟨-5,2,7⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩=30.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ ⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20,13,31⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,13,1)"] ["math" "(-20,13,31)"] ["math" "(-20,31,13)"] ["math" "(13,-20,31)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-20,13,31)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,2,-5)"] ["math" "(-7,4,-9)"] ["math" "(3,0,-1)"] ["math" "(8,-2,3)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-7,4,-9)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,-3,9)"] ["math" "(-6,-3,6)"] ["math" "(-9,-3,3)"] ["math" "(-9,-3,9)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-9,-3,9)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,2,7⟩+t⟨-5,-6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩=-24.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ ⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ -6(3-5t)+5(2-6t)+4\\cdot 7 & =-24 \\\\ -18+30t+10-30t+28 & =-24 \\\\ 20 & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-5,-6,0)"] ["math" "(-5,2,0)"] ["math" "(3,-6,7)"] ["math" "(3,2,7)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No intersection"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(5,-2,3)"] ["math" "(5,-5,4)"] ["math" "(5,-8,5)"] ["math" "(5,1,2)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5,-2,3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,1,-1)"] ["math" "(1,12,-18)"] ["math" "(1,2,-8)"] ["math" "(10,21,-14)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-74003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,12,-18)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(18,11,16)"] ["math" "(18,8,12)"] ["math" "(19,10,16)"] ["math" "(8,-1,6)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-73993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(18,11,16)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3y-4z & =-43 \\\\ 5(6+2t)+3(5+t)-4(-3-3t) & =-43 \\\\ 30+10t+15+3t+12+12t & =-43 \\\\ 25t & =-100 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2(-4) \\\\ y=5+(-4) \\\\ z=-3-3(-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-2,1,9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,1,9)"] ["math" "(2,3,3)"] ["math" "(4,4,0)"] ["math" "(8,6,-6)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108326" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-2,1,9)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,-1,5)"] ["math" "(1,0,4)"] ["math" "(11,5,-1)"] ["math" "(9,4,0)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1,-1,5)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,13,-3)"] ["math" "(-6,15,-2)"] ["math" "(18,-1,-10)"] ["math" "(3,9,-5)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-108337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-6,15,-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,1,0⟩+t⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,Π:3x-2y+4z+6=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,-5,0)"] ["math" "(-5,0,-4)"] ["math" "(0,-5,-4)"] ["math" "(3,-2,4)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,-5,-4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,-2,6⟩+t⟨2,5,4⟩,\\,Π:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ ⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,8,14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,-2,6)"] ["math" "(14,8,3)"] ["math" "(3,4,8)"] ["math" "(3,8,14)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,8,14)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2,8,7)"] ["math" "(3,4,4)"] ["math" "(7,2,8)"] ["math" "(7,8,2)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(7,8,2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-5,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,1,0⟩,\\,Π:-3x+y-2z+27=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+y-2z+27 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-2z & =-27 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ ⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ -3(-5-3t)+1\\cdot t-2\\cdot 1 & =-27 \\\\ 15+9t+t-2 & =-27 \\\\ 10t & =-40 \\\\ t & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-5-3(-4),-4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,-4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-8,1,1)"] ["math" "(1,-4,7)"] ["math" "(7,-4,1)"] ["math" "(7,1,-4)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(7,-4,1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-12,10,6⟩+s⟨1,0,4⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,4⟩\\times ⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-19,-5,-2)"] ["math" "(-2,9,-5)"] ["math" "(-5,-2,-1)"] ["math" "(-9,-5,-2)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "q-33968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-19,-5,-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fc63c3f8b83f5595a50eee33201f4aa628ca70f05da415fffd0d26fb175f8d1"} {"question" "e-4943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4943.json" "file_sha256" "8edb8a76fae66456c262e287e09ade8f215c09e2a407d5996a2845e67714ce3e"} {"question" "e-4943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4943.json" "file_sha256" "8edb8a76fae66456c262e287e09ade8f215c09e2a407d5996a2845e67714ce3e"} {"question" "e-4945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/assets/2a24a49f0fc47c235776597df655e75be9c68cffbb7988db16b36d9200f801bc.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4945.json" "file_sha256" "6a873b12172db6b35a2242763fe671613aeef836257fb9a54e5a36985334892e"} {"question" "e-4945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4945.json" "file_sha256" "6a873b12172db6b35a2242763fe671613aeef836257fb9a54e5a36985334892e"} {"question" "e-4944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4944.json" "file_sha256" "d9796b04b5eb6819adbc2727d2a4df50a56e1e44b90f1dcb63d9d778beadf4b8"} {"question" "e-4944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/example-4944.json" "file_sha256" "d9796b04b5eb6819adbc2727d2a4df50a56e1e44b90f1dcb63d9d778beadf4b8"}] "usage" {"e-4945" [] "e-4943" [] "e-4944" [] "q-33203" []} "basis" 1916 "retractions" [[17592186120172 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: r = ⟨ - 5, 0, 1⟩ + t⟨ - 3, 1, 0⟩, Π: - 3x + y - 2z + 27 = 0$."] [17592186119577 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65$."] [17592186119577 :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t, 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n⟨5 + 4t, 3 - 2t,-4 - 3t⟩ \\cdot ⟨ - 7, 5, 1⟩ &= -65 \\\\\n- 7(5 + 4t) + 5(3 - 2t) + (-4 - 3t) &= -65 \\\\\n- 35 - 28t + 15 - 10t - 4 - 3t &= -65 \\\\\n- 41t &= -41 \\\\\nt &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨5 + 4(1), 3 - 2(1),-4 - 3(1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨9, 1,-7⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9, 1, -7)$."] [17592186119579 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n${x = 3 - 4t; y =-1 + 2t; z = 2 + 3t$"] [17592186119579 :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 4y + 6z + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n3(3 - 4t) + 4(-1 + 2t) + 6(2 + 3t) + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n9 - 12t - 4 + 8t + 12 + 18t + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n14t &= -42 \\\\\nt &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{x = 3 - 4(-3) = 15; y =-1 + 2(-3) =-7; z = 2 + 3(-3) =-7\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7)$."] [17592186119578 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n$l: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0$."] [17592186119578 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 3y + 2z - 7 &= 0 \\\\\n4x - 3y + 2z &= 7 \\\\\n⟨x, y, z⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t, 3+t, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\ninto the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n⟨1 + 2t, 3 + t, 1⟩ \\cdot ⟨4,-3, 2⟩ &= 7 \\\\\n4(1 + 2t) - 3(3 + t) + 2 \\cdot 1 &= 7 \\\\\n4 + 8t - 9 - 3t + 2 &= 7 \\\\\n5t &= 10 \\\\\nt &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ⟨1 + 2(2), 3 + (2), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5, 5, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5, 5, 1)$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117553 17592186117554 17592186117555 17592186117556 17592186117557] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117552 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117552 :answer-field/id] [17592186117552 :answer-field/key] [17592186117552 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
